A||N||7||andrewbreen||1987 GT||||3||
Z||000000||andrewbreen||07-20-2000||11:29 PM||||Hey, I'm new here, so excuse me if this has been asked a million times. I recently got a 87 GT, its in great shape both in and out, and besides minor things needs no work. I want to upgrade both the look and performance of the car but not spend a fortune doing so. DO you have any suggestions on where to start? The car is completely stock, and i don't want to spend a any more then a few hundred per upgrade.<BR>Thanks in advance!||||reg||3
Z||000001||Ed||07-21-2000||01:25 AM||||Sway bar and urethane bushings on all bar attachment points front and rear.  <P>Whichever end doesn't have one!  Its been so long since I added the bar I can't remember which end doesn't come with one! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||07-21-2000||07:57 AM||||One of the cheapest upgrades you can do for performance and economy is get a K&N Filtercharger.  Actually improves airflow over having no filter at all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||07-21-2000||09:29 AM||||Check out the electronics on the car distributor,distributor cap, ignition coil, wires, spark pluges, pickup coil. If they are original, they are probably beat.  I had my original distributor in for 13 years it worked, but a new one made a world of difference in performance. ||||reg||3
Z||000004||DJRice||07-21-2000||09:39 AM||||ditto on what Lar said.<P>When I finally got around to doing a tune up on my 87, I had only had it about a year.  <BR>I discovered the forward 3 plugs were the original spark plugs (and I had a heckuva time getting them out).  <P>The lower temp thermostat and temp unit is a relatively cheap upgrage as well.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
Z||000005||RobertVol||07-21-2000||07:23 PM||||Also when checking Dist and all that check that dreaded O ring !!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3acb6910.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||andrewbreen||07-21-2000||09:06 PM||||Thanks for all your input! I am replacing all the ignition, spark plugs, etc.<BR>Has anyone had any positive/negative experinces with performance chips? i see the Fiero Store sells a few different ones, is one better then another?<P>Thanks Again!<BR>Andrew||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||07-21-2000||09:27 PM||||It's been proven that performance chips in a fiero don't make that much difference. The MSD ignition coil is a good upgrade for about $40. The part number is MSD #8226 in the Jegs catalog. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/firedup.txt</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-21-2000).]||||reg||1
